message: "If you use Hemolux in your research or clinical benchmarking, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Hemolux: Non-Invasive Conjunctival Pallor Screening with Fairness-Audited Selective Prediction"
version: "0.1.0-alpha"
date-released: 2024-10-05
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bhagyansh07/hemolux"
url: "https://hemolux.pages.dev"
authors:
  - family-names: "Research Team"
    given-names: "Hemolux"
    affiliation: "Hemolux Open Science Collaboration"
keywords:
  - "anaemia screening"
  - "conjunctival pallor"
  - "algorithmic fairness"
  - "selective prediction"
  - "ordinal classification"
  - "mobile health"
  - "edge AI"
  - "individual typology angle"
abstract: >-
  Hemolux is an edge-native, zero-cloud non-invasive conjunctival pallor screening
  system engineered for low-resource smartphone environments. It features an
  ordinal regression architecture, calibrated selective prediction (abstaining
  under adverse optical conditions), and comprehensive fairness auditing across
  skin phototypes (Individual Typology Angle).
